    "326365": {
      "mathdb_id": 326365,
      "title": "The structural conjecture for vertically 4-connected matroids with a modular 4-point line",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.5329",
      "literal": {
        "gate": "PASS_ALL20_PERSONALLY_READ_BEFORE_PRIORITY",
        "complete_statement": "Let $M$ be a simple, vertically $4$-connected matroid with a modular $4$-point line $L$.\n\n**Structural conjecture.** Either $M$ is ternary, for some $e\\in L$ the deletion $M\\backslash e$ is binary, or $M$ has an $F_7$-minor and either an $F_7^-$- or $(F_7^-)^*$-minor.\n\nThis conjecture proposes that, among simple vertically $4$-connected matroids with a modular $4$-point line, the known ternary case and the case obtained by deleting one element to obtain a binary matroid account for all possibilities apart from the specified $F_7$ and non-Fano minor configuration. The surrounding discussion presents it as a likely classification and does not state that it has been resolved.",
