    "327694": {
      "mathdb_id": 327694,
      "title": "Erd\u0151s's conjecture on odd cycle lengths in triangle-free graphs",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.4544",
      "literal": {
        "gate": "PASS_ALL20_PERSONALLY_READ_BEFORE_PRIORITY",
        "complete_statement": "Let $G$ be a triangle-free graph with chromatic number $k$, and let $\\frac{}{ }$ denote a positive real parameter. **Erd\u0151s's conjecture.** For every $\\frac{}{ } > 0$, there exists $k_0(\\frac{}{ })$ such that, for $k \\geq k_0(\\frac{}{ })$, every triangle-free $k$-chromatic graph contains more than $k^{2-\\frac{}{ }}$ odd cycles of different lengths.\n\nThe conjecture concerns how many distinct odd cycle lengths must occur in triangle-free graphs of large chromatic number. The paper proves a stronger result, namely that such graphs contain cycles of a quadratic-logarithmic number of consecutive lengths, so this conjecture is solved.",
