    "328748": {
      "mathdb_id": 328748,
      "title": "The full Erd\u0151s\u2013Ko\u2013Rado conjecture for t-intersecting perfect matchings",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.2057",
      "literal": {
        "gate": "PASS_ALL20_PERSONALLY_READ_BEFORE_PRIORITY",
        "complete_statement": "Let $K_{2n}$ be the complete graph on $2n$ vertices, and let $\\mathcal{F}$ be a family of its perfect matchings. The family is **$t$-intersecting** if $|m\\cap m'|>t$ for all $m,m'\\in\\mathcal{F}$. It is **trivially $t$-intersecting** when, for some collection $T$ of $t$ pairwise disjoint 2-sets of $[2n]$, \n$$\n\\mathcal{F}_T=\\{m\\in\\mathcal{M}_{2n}:T\\subseteq m\\}.\n$$\n **The full Erd\u0151s\u2013Ko\u2013Rado conjecture for t-intersecting perfect matchings.** If $\\mathcal{F}$ is a $t$-intersecting family of perfect matchings of $K_{2n}$, then \n$$\n|\\mathcal{F}|\\leq (2(n-t)-1)!!.\n$$\n Moreover, equality holds if and only if $\\mathcal{F}$ is trivially $t$-intersecting. This extends the known Erd\u0151s\u2013Ko\u2013Rado theorem for intersecting families of perfect matchings and remains an open generalization for $t$-intersecting families.",
        "provenance": "literal-provenance.json#328748"
      },
