    "329404": {
      "mathdb_id": 329404,
      "title": "Balogh, Kostochka and Treglown's degree-sequence Hajnal\u2013Szemer\u00e9di conjecture",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.1774",
      "literal": {
        "gate": "PASS_ALL20_PERSONALLY_READ_BEFORE_PRIORITY",
        "complete_statement": "Let $n,r\\in\\mathbb N$ with $r$ dividing $n$. Let $G$ be a graph on $n$ vertices with degree sequence $d_1\\leq\\dots\\leq d_n$. **Balogh, Kostochka and Treglown's conjecture.** If\n\n$$\nd_i\\geq (r-2)n/r+i\n$$\n\nfor all $i<n/r$, and\n\n$$\nd_{n/r+1}\\geq (r-1)n/r,\n$$\n\nthen $G$ contains a perfect $K_r$-packing. A perfect $K_r$-packing is a collection of vertex-disjoint copies of $K_r$ covering all vertices of $G$. This conjecture proposes a degree-sequence analogue of the Hajnal\u2013Szemer\u00e9di theorem, characterising sufficient degree conditions for a perfect clique packing; its resolution status is not specified in the source.",
